{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966787,"nonce":"k4wHnwMvdVR1ak7U45r7V43DhTE=","title":"(84ccd7eb): if/else in widget bodies now works; while-with-children still broken.","message":"Roadmap item \"full control flow within view bodies\". `Div(class=\"a\") { if cond { Div{…} } }` parses and compiles but renders **nothing** — a silent drop, no diagnostic. Measured with a layout-tree node count (validate the counter against a static baseline first, or \"1 node\" reads as a broken probe): static 1-child = 3 nodes, `if true { Div{Text} }` = 1 node, `while i\u003c3 {…}` = 1 node. `match` in a widget body doesn't even parse.\n\n**Cause 1 (Blinc-side, fixable).** `collect_children_into` in `passes/components.rs` (was passes.rs:2640 pre-split) partitions a widget's body block into a `children` **Array of expressions** via `let TypedStatement::Expression(e) = s.node else { continue };` — so every `if`/`while`/`match`/`let` statement is silently `continue`d. The grammar comment at `grammar/blinc.zyn` ~2202 claims the opposite (\"the Block variant carries an arbitrary statement list natively, so child rules like `let x = …`, `if cond { … }` … compose without bespoke wrappers\") — the Block does carry them, the consuming pass throws them away.\n\n**Cause 2 (NOT upstream — cause still unidentified).** Even with cause 1 fixed, children don't render. Observed: an `if` that is a **direct statement of the view fn body** executes (`view { if true { hit.set(42) } Div{…} }` → hit==42), but the same `if` spliced into the **block-expression** `lower_children_arrays_to_blocks` builds (`Block { let __list = __new_child_list__(); if c { __push_child__(__list, …) }; Div(children=__list) }`, in return/expression position) does not — no panic, side effects never fire.\n\nI initially blamed Zyntax's block-expression lowering. **That was wrong.** The PINNED rev (`9763886`) already handles this: `crates/compiler/src/ssa.rs:5074` `TypedExpression::Block` routes non-Expression/Let/Return statements through `process_statement` and consumes `continuation_block`, with a comment naming this exact bug as previously fixed (\"dropping it on the `_ =\u003e {}` floor … silently skipped both branches of every if-statement inside a closure\"). So the capability exists at the pinned rev and the real cause is elsewhere — most likely the Blinc-side transformation, or a different lowering path (`typed_cfg.rs:1078`/`1253` also match `TypedExpression::Block`). Re-investigate there; do not re-blame upstream without evidence.\n\n**DECISION (2026-07): stay on the pinned rev.** Blinc switches to upstream zyntax versions only once the local zyntax work AND the DSL work are complete. Do not bump the pin as a side quest — fix DSL issues against `9763886`. The bump feasibility below is recorded for when that time comes.\n\n**Bumping the zyntax pin is NOT blocked** (I first claimed it was — wrong). Patching to the local checkout initially errors on `libm` (`^0.2.16` from wasmtime-main cranelift 0.135 vs locked 0.2.15 via `naga \"=26.0.0\"`) and then `memmap2`, but both requirements are semver-COMPATIBLE — the errors are stale-`Cargo.lock` artifacts, not conflicts. A plain `cargo update` re-resolves: libm 0.2.15→0.2.16, memmap2 0.9.9→0.9.11, and every deliberate `=` pin holds (wgpu 26.0.1, naga 26.0.0, wgpu-hal 26.0.5, gpu-alloc 0.6.0). After that the only source break is **2 struct-literal sites** needing the new `TypedFunction.is_fiber: bool` field (`passes/consts.rs`, `lib.rs`, next to the existing `is_pure`). All 167 tests then pass against local zyntax HEAD.\n\nCaveat if bumping for real: local zyntax HEAD moves cranelift from crates.io `0.106` to `git wasmtime.git branch = \"main\"` (0.133/0.135) for \"newer mem2reg/GVN/LICM behavior on the SROA + LICM retry\" — a **branch** dep is unpinned, so the JIT backend can shift under you; pin it to a `rev` first. The 3 `#[ignore]`d lambda-return tests still FAIL at HEAD, so that upstream issue is genuinely unfixed. Working patch + resolved lockfile were saved to the session scratchpad (`zyntax-head-bump.patch`).\n\n`libm` purpose, for gating decisions: both consumers are `#![no_std]` crates using it as the pure-Rust libm replacement. naga uses exactly 2 call sites (`libm::rint`/`rintf` for the WGSL `round()` builtin in `proc/constant_evaluator.rs`, i.e. compile-time shader constant folding); cranelift-codegen uses 5 (`libm::pow` in `isa/riscv64/inst/args.rs`). Neither declares it `optional`, so there is nothing to feature-gate — and nothing needs gating, since one 0.2.16 satisfies both.\n\n**Implementation notes for the retry.** Carry the control-flow statement as a marker call `__cf_children__(Block{stmt})`, NOT a bare Block: a nested widget-with-children is itself lowered to a trailing-expression Block, so a bare Block in child position is ambiguous and splicing it destroys nested composition (this regressed `jit_view_renderer_div_nested_div_composes`, `example_counter_dsl_compiles`, `example_reactive_dsl_compiles`, `core_layout_widgets_compile_and_return_element_builders`). `rewrite_expr` recurses into Call positional args, so a marker call still gets its inner widgets expanded post-order. Discriminator for \"this statement produces a child\": `Expression(Call)` (leaf widget) or `Expression(Block)` (already-expanded widget-with-children); `MethodCall` (`sig.set(…)`) is a side effect and must stay untouched so `while c { Row{…} i.set(i.get()+1) }` both emits and advances. Do NOT carry `let` — earlier passes hoist bindings and wrapping them changes scope.\n\n**Path forward:** hoist the children prelude to the enclosing *statement* level instead of wrapping it in a block-expression (emit `let __list = …; if c { push }` as statements of the containing fn, leaving only the widget call in expression position). That sidesteps the upstream limitation entirely, since function-body blocks execute `If` correctly. Alternative is fixing Zyntax's block-expression codegen upstream — note Blinc is pinned 218 commits behind zyntax HEAD (`9763886`).\n\nSame upstream family as the deferred `for` loop: `grammar/blinc.zyn` ~1483 disables `for_stmt`/`range_expr` because `compiler/cfg.rs::process_for_loop` builds header→body→header with True/False edges but never emits the has-next check or induction variable, so the body loops forever. `Let` and `Block` ARE constructible in the action language (`zyn_peg/src/runtime2/interpreter.rs:532`/`632`), so `for x in a..b` can be desugared to `Let`+`While` purely in the Blinc grammar once the block-expression issue above is resolved. Related: gotcha zyntax lambda return value, gotcha zyntax closure body control flow.\n\n\n**RESOLVED for `if`/`else` — commit 84ccd7eb.** Three fixes were needed together:\n\n1. **Blinc `collect_children_into` (passes/components.rs)** — carry `If`/`While` statements in child position as a `__cf_children__(Block{stmt})` MARKER CALL, not a bare Block (a nested widget-with-children is itself lowered to a trailing-expression Block, so a bare Block is ambiguous; splicing it destroys nested composition and regressed 4 tests on the first attempt). `lower_children_arrays_to_blocks` (passes/widgets.rs) recognises the marker, rewrites child-producing calls inside into `__push_child__` against the hoisted list, and splices the statements into the prelude — preserving source order.\n2. **Child discriminator must be semantic, not structural.** Only `…$view`-producing calls (or a Block whose trailing expr is one) count as children. `Expression(Call)` alone is WRONG: by that stage `sig.set(v)` is a bare `__signal_set_by_id_*` call with a VOID result, and wrapping it in `__push_child__` fed codegen a void argument → Cranelift \"arg not in value_map\" abort. Also `walk_stmt` had to recurse into `While`/`Block` so a widget nested in a loop body gets its own children expanded.\n3. **zyntax `ssa.rs` block-expression arm must publish its continuation** (patch saved at `scratchpad/zyntax-control-flow-fixes.patch`, NOT committed — user's repo). Control-flow statements inside a value-position Block carve new blocks, so translation migrates out of `block_id` into `current`; without setting `self.continuation_block = Some(current)`, the caller's `Return` terminator landed on the ORIGINAL block and overwrote the `CondBranch` — silently killing both arms. Same patch adds an on-demand `TypedStatement::While` arm to `process_statement` (there was none; the catch-all dropped the whole loop).\n\n**STILL BROKEN: `while` with children.** The loop runs correctly in a widget body when the body has no child push (side-effect-only body reaches 3 iterations), and the emitted IR is textbook — header with back-edge, `Div$view` + `__push_child__` + signal set in the body. But adding ANY child push (even a leaf `Text`) zeroes the iterations silently. Isolated cause: the child list is defined in the ENTRY block and the loop body's cross-block use of it fails — same class as the `value_map` panic, which the discriminator fix only sidestepped. Start there; do NOT re-investigate the loop shape or the While arm, both verified correct via CFG + instruction dump (`ZDUMP` env-gated dump in cranelift_backend around `compute_block_order` is the technique).\n\nBonus bug this surfaced: the grammar's builtin-extern table declared i32/f64/string signal accessors but **not bool**, so a `bool` read inside `computed { … } : bool` failed lowering with \"Call to undefined function\". Latent until 16abb4c3 made computed bodies actually reach lowering.\n\n**Follow-up (cc611f22): a widget body may contain non-child statements.** The child/side-effect discriminator was applied inside control-flow carriers but NOT in the straight-line child loop, so `Div { sig.set(5) Text(\"x\") }` — no control flow, single file — pushed the void `__signal_set_by_id_*` call as a child and aborted codegen with \"arg not in value_map\". Both paths now share `is_widget_producing_expr` (only `…$view` calls, or a Block whose trailing expr is one). When touching either path, change both.\n\n**Cross-module props already work** (verified, `tests/cross_module_props.rs`): one prop arrives, two keep their order. The old `inject_imported_view_externs` doc claiming \"zero-prop only\" was stale — the synthesized extern genuinely has no param list, but `lower_component_calls` positionalises args against the component's signature from its compiled module, so the declaration's arity is not what's consulted.\n\n**`while`-with-children remains broken** and is NOT the same bug as the above: after cc611f22 there is no panic, but iterations are still zero (side-effect-only loop bodies DO run — reaching 3 — so the loop machinery itself is fine). Rejected hypothesis: loop-header sealing. My `While` arm seals header/body/exit up front, which is wrong in general SSA (a header's back-edge predecessor arrives later), but it is NOT the cause here because the arm explicitly inherits `definitions` into the body, so the child-list variable resolves without needing a phi. Next angle: why a `__push_child__` in the body specifically prevents entry, given the emitted IR and CFG are both verified correct.","files":null}]}